                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Final Fantasy X is a masterpiece that will always have a special place in my heart.\nIt was was the first Final Fantasy game I ever played on the PS2, and I fell in love with it from the very beginning. There was something truly magical about this game that hooked me completely: the story, the characters, the aesthetics, the soundtrack, and the breathtaking environments. Its not just a game, its its an unforgettable experience that stayed with me for years.\nthe story... oh, the story.  THis game is an emotional journey filled with love, sacrifice, friendship, faith, and the struggle against impossible circumstances. \nI must admit that I've cried more than once while playing this game, even though I've beaten it MAAAAANY times throughout my life. Somehow, knowing what's coming next in the storyline  doesn't make the emotional moments less powerful. If anything. The ending still hits me right in the heart every single time. 😭\nThe ost deserves special recognition, too. Nobuo Uematsu and the other composers created something really  unforgettable, with tracks that perfectly expres the emotions and atmosphere. The song To Zanarkand is absolutely legendary, and just hearing a few notes can bring me back so many memories.\nAbout the gameplay, the turn-based combat system is a classic from ff series, which i  really enjoy. The ability to switch party members during battle,, and the sfereGrid system make combat satisfying and rewarding.\nThe only “flaws” is that is kinda hard to get all the supreme weapons at max level, specially tidus”s weapon and wakka”s. The chocobo race in calm lands freaked me out for hours and still couldnt complete it to get the item yo upgrade tidus weapon.Also to enhance wakka´s weapon you must beat the blitzball tournament, which felt impossible for me since the mechanics are odd.\nDespite all of that, i enthusiastically recommend this game to anyone who loves classic JRPGs, emotionally engaging storytelling, beautiful environments, memorable soundtracks, strategic turn-based combat, and characters with genuine personalities and individuality.\nFinal Fantasy X isn't simply a game; it's a piece of my  gaming history that I'll always cherish. It's one of those rare experiences that reminds you why you fell in love with video games in the first place. If you haven't played it yet, please give it a chance. Join tidus and the others  to defeat Sinh  save Spira!!\n….listen to my story.. This may be our last chance\n",
